{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794389843,"nonce":"WjZlPVfuUeEt3JxVN7cqzid4U7o=","message":"Measured after the gaps closed (69f9d628). Mac, release ash, single runs; load1 was 8-14 during an earlier pass and 31-55 during this one, so wall times here are inflated and user CPU is the steadier column. NUC not used, so none of this is confirmed on Linux.\n\nConformance (unit, 1069 cases / 10971 assertions): 1069/1069 and 10971/10971 for ASH_WASM_DIRECT=only and =1, each on wasm and wasm-fibers.\n\nBuild, user CPU / wall (LLVM -\u003e mixed -\u003e only):\n- hello: 1.6s -\u003e 0.3s -\u003e 0.07s CPU; wall 0.95 -\u003e 0.18 -\u003e 0.12\n- unit (8688 functions): 120s -\u003e 17s -\u003e 4.1s CPU; wall 48 -\u003e 15 -\u003e 4.2 (63 -\u003e 19 -\u003e 3.6 at load ~12)\n- unit with fibers: 120s -\u003e 18s -\u003e 4.9s CPU; wall 48 -\u003e 16 -\u003e 5.2\n- Pocket Studio (4038 functions): 44.6s -\u003e 9.9s -\u003e 3.1s CPU; wall 15.7 -\u003e 7.3 -\u003e 3.3; with fibers 42.5 -\u003e 11.1 -\u003e 4.0 CPU, wall 14.1 -\u003e 8.9 -\u003e 4.8\nModule size: unit 20.5 -\u003e 13.4 -\u003e 12.4 MB (fibers 28.3 -\u003e 22.0 -\u003e 20.9); Pocket 12.8 -\u003e 11.1 -\u003e 10.2 MB (fibers 17.2 -\u003e 15.1 -\u003e 13.9).\n\nCold launch (wasmtime compile + start), unit: no fibers 10.1s -\u003e 7.6s -\u003e 7.2s CPU (wall 2.4 -\u003e 2.0 -\u003e 1.9). With fibers it is WORSE: 33s -\u003e 63s -\u003e 65s CPU (wall 8.6 -\u003e 17.7 -\u003e 18.4). Warm launch with fibers 0.38s -\u003e 0.33s -\u003e 0.32s. hello cold launch is the same across all three.\n\nWhy the fiber compile is slower: the module has 2.3x the locals per function (8.5 vs 3.6; 6.3 vs 3.6 after dropping unused bookkeeping locals) and the fiber transform restores every local at each resume point. sum(locals x call sites) 5.0M vs 3.2M for LLVM. Trimming bookkeeping locals and moving constants to data (the 936 KB start-up function) did not close it. Open: save only live locals in the transform, or reduce locals further.\n\nSpeed (bench): fib 178-194ms -\u003e 80-90ms; loopSum without fibers 618 -\u003e 345-384ms, with fibers 462 -\u003e 555ms (+20%); grid within noise.\n\nStill LLVM-only: host exports/closures/object tails+drops/host-linked natives (embedder API only; the CLI passes none).","files":null}]}